Z||000003||theogre||01-02-2000||12:25 AM||||What year motor and tranny is this?<P>While there is no driveshaft as you mean it there are 2 "half shafts" that go from the tranny to the wheels.<P>A motor mount or "dog bone" bushing could also be bad. The dog bone is almost guarteed shot it it's not one of the urethane solutions. Could also be a "cradle bushing", especially on a manual tranny car.<P>If this is a 4 cyl check the air cleaner and trunk wall for signs they've hit. If they have replace the gasket under the throttle body unit. You may as well rebuild the TBI unit at that time. the rebuild "kit" is about 30-40$us. ((If this is an 86.5 or latter 4 cyl/auto tranny with only on tranny mount then you can about bet the air cleaner has whacked the trunk and messed the TB gasket.))<P><BR>The "oxidation" you describe is likely a failed "clear coat" layer. It cannot be removed without sanding or scraping. A complete repair requires repainting the pannel. The clear coat fails as a result of heat, sunlight(UV) exposure, and acid rain.<P>If this is a black car there is a temporary fix. Carefully wet sand the clear coat off with 600 or finer paper. Use care not to got thru the paint. Then after the clear coat flakes are gone get some black paste shoe polish. (Shoe polish is related to car polish, but in this case if you use car polish you will fill the sanding scratches with a residue you will see. You'll never buff enough to get the white/light color residue out of the scratches.) Apply the polish and buff the heck out of it. It won't be as good as a paint job, but it looks far better than the dandruff you have now. ((I supose if you can find a dyed car polish you could do this to colored paint.))<P>If you aren't very carefull you'll know. The plastic and primer will show real quick. you'll have to paint then. ((Unless it's a black car, in what case the primer and plastic lid are also black. They'll still show but not as obvious once they are buffed.))<P>I did this to my own car and was suprised how well it worked out. It's not a new paint job, but now it doesn't look like it was snowed on year round. The black cars tend to get this really bad. not just the lid but the rear quarter panel tops and the back part of the roof as well. It looks really bad.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-02-2000).]||||reg||1
