Z||000014||theogre||01-03-2000||09:37 PM||||Annie, what tranny is in it? an automatic?<P>If it is an auto, look at the tranny and see if it has a big metal bracket wrapped around it with on rubber mount under it. The mount will be in between the tranny and the strut tower.<P>If the tranny has this mount it will transmit signifigantly more vibration to the car than the older ones that have 2 mounts, one in front of and on behind the tranny. Adding a Urethane dogbone to it makes it even worse. Not so bad you can't drive but you will notice it.<P>On the other hand, the urethane dogbone bushings are the only ones strong enough for the single mount tranny setup. The OEM rubber ones will be shreaded in about a year.<P>The reason is that the older 2 mount setup is providing additional torque damping. The new style single mount only holds up the tranny.<P>All the manual transmision cars have the 2 mount setup.||||reg||1
